Below is an outline of how you might structure a Java-based backend service meeting these requirements. This example uses Spring Boot for building RESTful services and WebSocket support, RabbitMQ for message queuing, and a simplified approach for integrating external notifications.

### 1. Set Up Project

Create a new Spring Boot project with dependencies: `spring-boot-starter-web`, `spring-boot-starter-websocket`, `spring-boot-starter-actuator`, `spring-boot-starter-amqp` (for RabbitMQ), and your preferred database starter.

